        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: William A. Wellman, Ginger Rogers, Adolphe Menjou, George Montgomery, Nigel Bruce, Phil Silvers, William Frawley, Spring Byington\n- Products: Roxie Hart\n- Topics: American comedy films, entertainers, comedic actors\n\nFacts:\n- Roxie Hart, also known as Chicago or Chicago Gal, is a 1942 American comedy film.\n- William A. Wellman directed the 1942 American comedy film Roxie Hart.\n- Ginger Rogers, Adolphe Menjou, George Montgomery, Nigel Bruce, Phil Silvers, William Frawley, and Spring Byington starred in Roxie Hart.\n- Phil Silvers was born on May 11, 1911.\n- Phil Silvers was an American entertainer and comedic actor.\n- Phil Silvers was known as \"The King of Chutzpah\".\n- Phil Silvers died on November 1, 1985.",
